  "publishedAt": "2026-10-10T09:01:45.000Z",
  "contentHtml": "<figure><a href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!w6Is!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5de5d442-0449-4f37-a82b-7e09457b3074_2756x748.png\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!w6Is!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5de5d442-0449-4f37-a82b-7e09457b3074_2756x748.png\" width=\"1456\" height=\"395\" data-size=\"normal\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></figure>\n<p><span>In this space on Saturdays, I </span><a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/t/roundup\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">do a weekly round-up</a><span> of sorts: Sifting through what I wrote that you might have missed during the week, what I’ve been reading and watching myself, and some other fun things that have been going on.</span></p>\n<hr>\n<h4>📝 What I did this week</h4>\n<p><em>Here are the things I wrote or podcasted about during the previous week, sorted in descending order by quality, popularity and/or current relevance.</em></p>\n<p><strong><span>📊 My </span><a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/t/updating-model\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Odds/Models</a><span>: </span><a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/2026-nfl-odds-tracker-and-elo-ratings\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">NFL </a></strong><span>| </span><strong><a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/2026-mlb-elo-power-ratings-playoff\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">MLB </a></strong><span>| </span><strong><a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/2026-wnba-elo-team-power-rankings\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">WNBA </a></strong><span>| </span><strong><a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/2026-27-nba-elo-forecast-and-player\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">NBA</a></strong><span> | </span><strong><a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/2026-27-nhl-team-elo-power-rankings\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">NHL </a></strong><span>| </span><strong><a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/2026-college-football-odds-tracker\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">CFB</a></strong><span> | </span><strong><a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/2026-27-english-premier-league-tracker\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">EPL</a><span> | </span><a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/2026-nascar-cup-series-driver-rankings\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">NASCAR</a></strong></p>\n<ul><li><p><span>I officially started contributing my charts to the </span><strong><a href=\"https://yahoosports.com/am?.tsrc=1317&amp;ncid=crm_-2348335-20261009-1--A&amp;utm_content=mktg_1317_di_-2348335-20261009-1--A&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=email&amp;bt_user_id=SrjGgvZlBf5qIZUVu7yYI1CqlkUyD55KDXbV%2BKpd15uedTV17eKJtcMAhxssnZ11ayDylgxSDVgRNS4WgjqkPZPBV36yuhe3WjW0KlumYYM0G8xcJYj%2F85w0Ks9Zo1at&amp;bt_ts=1791548043236\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Yahoo! Sports AM newsletter</a></strong><span> this week! 🎉 Check out </span><strong><a href=\"https://view.newsletters.yahoo.net/messages/1791548043235b3fbc2173d5b/raw#:~:text=The%20following%20story%20is%20written%20by%20Neil%20Paine\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">this thing I did on Lane Johnson’s outsized impact on the Eagles’ offense</a></strong><span> Friday.</span></p></li><li><p><span>⚾ </span><strong><a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/why-should-dodgers-brewers-part-ii\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Why Should Dodgers-Brewers Part II Be Any Different?</a></strong><span> - Ahead of the dreaded NLCS rematch between Los Angeles and Milwaukee, I broke down why the Brewers once again possess a statistically compelling case to beat the Dodgers on paper… and whether regular-season data superiority means </span><em>anything</em><span> after last October’s historically one-sided Dodger sweep.</span></p></li><li><p><span>⚾ </span><strong><a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/yoshinobu-yamamoto-is-speedrunning\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Yoshinobu Yamamoto Is Speedrunning October Greatness</a></strong><span> - Following his </span><a href=\"https://www.baseball-reference.com/boxes/ATL/ATL202610060.shtml\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">dominant 10-strikeout gem against the Braves</a><span> in Game 3 of the NLDS, I examined how Yoshinobu Yamamoto is rapidly establishing one of the most impressive postseason resumes in modern baseball history, just three years into his MLB career.</span></p></li><li><p><span>⚾ </span><strong><a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/the-yankees-dynasty-began-with-players\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">The Yankees’ Dynasty Began With Players Who Wouldn’t Stick Around for Long </a></strong><span>- Thirty years after New York’s 1996 World Series championship run, I re-examined the roster that launched baseball’s last true dynasty — and why that team depended more heavily on short-term contributors (like </span><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Lac2R8qwTyw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">horse-riding Wade Boggs</a><span>, Kenny Rogers and Doc Gooden) than almost any other team that set a dynasty’s foundation in MLB history.</span></p></li><li><p><span>🏈 </span><strong><a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/rb-gravity-is-catching-up-with-saquon\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">RB Gravity Is Catching Up With Saquon Barkley — But Flags Fly Forever </a></strong><span>- After Saquon Barkley went down with a hamstring injury against the Rams, I looked at how the harsh aging curve of elite running backs is catching up with Philadelphia’s star — while also noting how his magical 2024 championship season already delivered the ultimate prize no matter what happens from here.</span></p></li><li><p><span>⚾ </span><strong><a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/guardians-white-sox-is-octobers-battle\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Guardians-White Sox Is October’s Battle of the Kids</a></strong><span> - As the two AL Central rivals clash in the Division Series, I examined the historic youth behind both rosters — featuring the youngest pair of lineups to ever meet in a Division Series — and what this unexpected playoff matchup reveals about their future beyond 2026.</span></p></li><li><p><span>🏀 </span><strong><a href=\"https://www.espn.com/wnba/story/_/id/50070477/aja-wilson-mvp-five-wnba-las-vegas-aces\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">A’ja Wilson is a five-time MVP! How does her run compare?</a></strong><span> - After it was announced Wilson had won the 2026 WNBA MVP (no surprise there), I compared her run of MVP-winning to other great stretches from throughout pro sports history:</span></p><div id=\"datawrapper-iframe\" class=\"reader-datawrapper\"><a href=\"https://datawrapper.dwcdn.net/Q1NPV/2/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/7dcbc6a3-9a7f-4b49-98fa-17980372359c_1220x864.png\" alt=\"Only GOATs win 4 MVPs in 5 years\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a><p>Only GOATs win 4 MVPs in 5 years</p></div></li><li><p><span>🏁 </span><strong><a href=\"https://www.nascar.com/news-media/2026/10/08/analysis-is-charlotte-denny-hamlins-last-stand/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Is Charlotte Denny Hamlin’s last stand?</a></strong><span> - At </span><span><a href=\"https://open.substack.com/users/99075140-nascar?utm_source=mentions\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">NASCAR</a></span><span> this week, I analyzed why Denny Hamlin’s elusive 22-year Cup Series pursuit of a championship seems destined to be unfilled this season, looking at why the Charlotte looms as maybe the last stand of a once-promising campaign for the No. 11 team.</span></p><ul><li><p><span>🏁🎙️ </span><strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/episode/4kV1P7ac2vChxtn0NeoVJR?si=z8H_rUQIRuGBGnS8R15pDQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Podracing: Denny goes bust</a></strong><span> - In this week’s </span><span><a href=\"https://open.substack.com/users/146677251-podracing?utm_source=mentions\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Podracing</a></span><span>, </span><span><a href=\"https://open.substack.com/users/845401-tyler?utm_source=mentions\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Tyler</a></span><a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/tyler-lauletta-b0399667/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"> Lauletta</a><span> and I talked about Chase Briscoe’s race for redemption at Vegas, Kyle Larson’s incredible comeback to nearly snatch away victory — and then finish-line-crossing wreck with Tyler Reddick — and why Hamlin’s chances are fading fast, despite everything seemingly being in his favor this year. Finally, we look ahead to Charlotte, the last of the 3x mile-and-a-halfs that we promised would define this year’s Chase.</span></p></li></ul></li></ul>\n<h4>📊 Charts of the week:</h4>\n<p><span>Here were some of my favorite viz items of the week from </span><em><strong><a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/scoreboard-newsletter-archives\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Scoreboard</a></strong></em><span>, my daily newsletter for </span><a href=\"https://sherwood.news/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Sherwood News</a><span>… </span></p>\n<p><strong>⚾</strong><em><strong><span> On the </span><a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/playoff-energy\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">White Sox’s wacky no-starters playoff pitching</a><span> strategy…</span></strong></em></p>\n<div id=\"datawrapper-iframe\" class=\"reader-datawrapper\"><a href=\"https://datawrapper.dwcdn.net/AFhqO/2/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/450f5e3a-0dc5-4cac-add9-cf1bc1113d1d_1220x2278.png\" alt=\"How each remaining playoff team has been using their postseason pitchers\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a><p>How each remaining playoff team has been using their postseason pitchers</p></div>\n<p><span>🏈</span><strong> </strong><em><strong><span>On the </span><a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/playoff-energy\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">highest-ranked combined matchups</a><span> in CFB…</span></strong></em></p>\n<div id=\"datawrapper-iframe\" class=\"reader-datawrapper\"><a href=\"https://datawrapper.dwcdn.net/PucfM/1/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/d76d217f-ccc0-4919-8f83-d9557f18e3b7_1220x1672.png\" alt=\"The best ranked matchups of the 2026 CFB season\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a><p>The best ranked matchups of the 2026 CFB season</p></div>\n<p><span>⚾</span><strong> </strong><em><strong><span>On Yamamoto’s place </span><a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/elimination-wednesday\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">on the all-time playoff Game Score list</a><span>…</span></strong></em></p>\n<div id=\"datawrapper-iframe\" class=\"reader-datawrapper\"><a href=\"https://datawrapper.dwcdn.net/Yji6r/1/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/57ddfeb5-ce42-4b48-a679-930a2bfad258_1220x1238.png\" alt=\"Yamamoto keeps adding to his postseason résumé\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a><p>Yamamoto keeps adding to his postseason résumé</p></div>\n<p><strong>🏈</strong><em><strong><span> On turnarounds (like the Falcons’) </span><a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/october-gets-real\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">associated with new QBs</a><span>…</span></strong></em></p>\n<div id=\"datawrapper-iframe\" class=\"reader-datawrapper\"><a href=\"https://datawrapper.dwcdn.net/WOgIP/1/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/3a45ecfc-7bef-4881-afa1-3632e4dfe821_1220x1094.png\" alt=\"These turnarounds were associated with new QBs\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a><p>These turnarounds were associated with new QBs</p></div>\n<p><span>⚾</span><em><strong><span> On the </span><a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/october-gets-real\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Yankees’ playoff error-fest</a><span>…</span></strong></em></p>\n<div id=\"datawrapper-iframe\" class=\"reader-datawrapper\"><a href=\"https://datawrapper.dwcdn.net/QoSkH/1/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/30a8dd69-002e-4986-aaec-1341c5f2d8ec_1220x1874.png\" alt=\"The errors of their ways\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a><p>The errors of their ways</p></div>\n<p><em><span>Subscribe to </span><strong>Scoreboard</strong><span> by </span><strong><a href=\"https://join.sherwood.news/scoreboard\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">clicking here</a></strong><span>!</span></em></p>\n<h4>👀 Some interesting things I read/watched this week</h4>\n<p><em>A collection of articles (with a heavy focus on my fellow Substackers), videos and other media that I enjoyed and/or found thought-provoking over the past week. I don’t always 100% agree with or endorse what’s linked here… but that’s also sort of the point.</em></p>\n<ul><li><p><strong><span>📺 </span><a href=\"https://www.imightbewrong.org/p/why-does-every-insurance-company?utm_source=post-email-title&amp;publication_id=375183&amp;post_id=218433685&amp;utm_campaign=email-post-title&amp;isFreemail=true&amp;r=gwh9&amp;triedRedirect=true&amp;utm_medium=email\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">“Why Does Every Insurance Company Have an Expansive, Tolkien-esque Universe of Mascots?”</a></strong><span>by </span><span><a href=\"https://open.substack.com/users/11145646-jeff-maurer?utm_source=mentions\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Jeff Maurer</a></span><span> - </span><em><strong>Note: </strong><span>Very pertinent if you watch sports for, like, 2 seconds or longer</span></em></p></li><li><p><strong><span>🏈 </span><a href=\"https://throwbacks.substack.com/p/brock-purdy-is-the-abba-of-quarterbacks?utm_source=post-email-title&amp;publication_id=31587&amp;post_id=219443991&amp;utm_campaign=email-post-title&amp;isFreemail=false&amp;r=gwh9&amp;triedRedirect=true&amp;utm_medium=email\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">“Brock Purdy Is the ABBA of Quarterbacks”</a></strong><span> and </span><strong><a href=\"https://throwbacks.substack.com/p/the-raiders-are-maybe-good-again?utm_source=post-email-title&amp;publication_id=31587&amp;post_id=219130540&amp;utm_campaign=email-post-title&amp;isFreemail=false&amp;r=gwh9&amp;triedRedirect=true&amp;utm_medium=email\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">“The Raiders Are (Maybe) Good Again. But They’ll Never Be the Raiders Again.”</a></strong><span>by </span><span><a href=\"https://open.substack.com/users/271632-michael-weinreb?utm_source=mentions\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Michael Weinreb</a></span></p></li><li><p><strong><span>🏈 </span><a href=\"https://thespade.substack.com/p/the-first-batch-of-transfer-portal?utm_source=post-email-title&amp;publication_id=1892935&amp;post_id=218846635&amp;utm_campaign=email-post-title&amp;isFreemail=true&amp;r=gwh9&amp;triedRedirect=true&amp;utm_medium=email\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">“The First Batch of Transfer Portal Predictions”</a></strong><span>by </span><span><a href=\"https://open.substack.com/users/26279421-ray-carpenter?utm_source=mentions\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ray Carpenter</a></span></p></li><li><p><span>🏈 </span><strong><a href=\"https://bfarrell27.substack.com/p/cfb-after-5-weeks-chip-kellys-comeback?utm_source=post-email-title&amp;publication_id=459537&amp;post_id=219007272&amp;utm_campaign=email-post-title&amp;isFreemail=true&amp;r=gwh9&amp;triedRedirect=true&amp;utm_medium=email\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">“CFB after 5 weeks: Chip Kelly’s comeback and more”</a></strong><span> by </span><span><a href=\"https://open.substack.com/users/15975019-brendan-farrell?utm_source=mentions\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Brendan Farrell</a></span></p></li><li><p><span>🏈 </span><strong><a href=\"https://badsport.substack.com/p/week-4-recap-yes-all-refs?utm_source=post-email-title&amp;publication_id=1013059&amp;post_id=219350345&amp;utm_campaign=email-post-title&amp;isFreemail=true&amp;r=gwh9&amp;triedRedirect=true&amp;utm_medium=email\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">“Week 4 Recap: Yes All Refs - On inevitability, short kings, and accountability.”</a></strong><span> by </span><span><a href=\"https://open.substack.com/users/15819470-elana-desantis?utm_source=mentions\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Elana DeSantis</a></span></p></li><li><p><strong><span>🏈 </span><a href=\"https://www.burdsofafeather.com/p/lane-johnson-was-the-great-wall-of?utm_source=post-email-title&amp;publication_id=5933793&amp;post_id=219248834&amp;utm_campaign=email-post-title&amp;isFreemail=true&amp;r=gwh9&amp;triedRedirect=true&amp;utm_medium=email\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">“Lane Johnson was the Great Wall of Philadelphia”</a></strong><span> by </span><span><a href=\"https://open.substack.com/users/14704668-jeremy-keys?utm_source=mentions\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Jeremy Keys</a></span></p></li><li><p><span>🏈 </span><strong><a href=\"https://alertthepost.substack.com/p/kalen-deboers-pass-attack?utm_source=post-email-title&amp;publication_id=1496903&amp;post_id=218864311&amp;utm